[0.001, "o", "I checked the dataset's list of columns and its list of things it doesn't contain, and didn't run any queries. The data can't       \r\nidentify red sports cars or show how police treat drivers outside of crashes.                                                       \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "No. This dataset cannot answer the question. SWITRS has no vehicle color column; the makes 'white' and 'bluebird' are manufacturers,\r\nnot colors. It also records only vehicle make and model year, not model or body style, so 'sports cars' can't be identified.        \r\nFinally, it contains only police-reported crashes. It has no traffic stops or tickets outside crashes, and no data on how many of   \r\neach kind of vehicle are on the road, which you would need to test for bias. Even a comparison of officer at-fault rates by make    \r\nwould only describe a pattern and could not show bias, because the data is observational.                                           \r\n\r\n\u001b[1mNot in the data\u001b[0m                                                                                                                     \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe data does not record vehicle color.                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe data records vehicle make and model year only, "]
[0.000, "o", "not model or body style (so not 'sports car').                                \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mTesting police bias needs stop and exposure data the file does not have. An at-fault comparison here is descriptive only.        \r\n\r\n\u001b[1mCaveats\u001b[0m                                                                                                                             \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe data covers 2001-01-01 to 2021-06-03.                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mOnly crashes reported to police are in the data.                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThis is observational data. Differences between groups can come from other factors and do not by themselves show cause.          \r\n\r\n\u001b[3mCheck: Claims bound to query cells: each number is the stated operation on the cited result cells, with the stated entity and \u001b[0m      \r\n\u001b[3mdirection. This does not prove a query measures what the question asks. Re"]
[0.000, "o", "view the query plans and SQL. Dataset \u001b[0m                    \r\n\u001b[3mswitrs-v6-b72ee1f04808, turn t1-9d3f.\u001b[0m                                                                                               \r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2mbackend sdk  |  5 model turns  |  22s  |  $0.200 est.  |  trace outputs/traces/cli-20261019-161628.jsonl\u001b[0m\r\n"]
